the target language is: prolog.

% The library of the Rune twins: the operations of Rune's expression
% language that are not a condition of their own in Logical English (the
% only element of a list, its distinct values, ...), and the functions DRR
% implements in Java rather than in Rune. Written for the translator of
% migration/rune (its README.md). The builder copies both files beside
% every twin it writes.

the knowledge base rune includes these resources:
    rune.pl.

the templates are:
    the only element of *a list* is *a value*.
    the first element of *a list* is *a value*.
    the last element of *a list* is *a value*.
    the least of *a list* is *a value*.
    the value or nothing of *a list* is *a value*.
    the element of *a list* with the least of the keys *a second list* is *a value*.
    the element of *a list* with the greatest of the keys *a second list* is *a value*.
    the elements of *a list* sorted by the keys *a second list* are *a third list*.
    the greatest of *a list* is *a value*.
    the distinct values of *a list* are *a second list*.
    the reverse of *a list* is *a second list*.
    the sorted values of *a list* are *a second list*.
    the concatenation of *a text* and *a second text* is *a third text*.
    the text of *a value* is *a text*.
    the number of *a value* is *a number*.
    *a list* contains every element of *a second list*.
    *a list* shares no element with *a second list*.
    *a value* comes before *a second value*.
    the joining of *a list* with *a separator* is *a text*.
    the time of the report is *a time*.
    *a text* contains the text *a second text*.
    the date *a date* plus *a number* days is *a second date*.
    the date part of *a time* is *a date*.
    the time part of *a time* is *a time of day*.
    the time zone part of *a time* is *a zone*.
    the year part of *a date* is *a year*.
    the month part of *a date* is *a month*.
    the day part of *a date* is *a day*.
    the day of the week of *a date* is *a day*.
    the days from *a date* to *a second date* are *a number*.
    the leap days from *a date* to *a second date* are *a number*.
    the number *a number* rounded to *a precision* decimal places towards *a direction* is *a value*.
    the number *a number* rounded to *a count* significant figures towards *a direction* is *a value*.
    the object built at *a site* with *an input* with *a second input* with *a third input* with *a fourth input* with *a fifth input* with *a sixth input* with *a seventh input* with *an eighth input* is *a value*.
    the object built at *a site* with *an input* with *a second input* with *a third input* with *a fourth input* with *a fifth input* with *a sixth input* with *a seventh input* is *a value*.
    the object built at *a site* with *an input* with *a second input* with *a third input* with *a fourth input* with *a fifth input* with *a sixth input* is *a value*.
    the object built at *a site* with *an input* with *a second input* with *a third input* with *a fourth input* with *a fifth input* is *a value*.
    the object built at *a site* with *an input* with *a second input* with *a third input* with *a fourth input* is *a value*.
    the object built at *a site* with *an input* with *a second input* with *a third input* is *a value*.
    the object built at *a site* with *an input* with *a second input* is *a value*.
    the object built at *a site* with *an input* is *a value*.
    the object built at *a site* is *a value*.

the knowledge base rune includes:

% Rune's only-element: the value of a list of exactly one value.
the only element of a list is a value if
    prolog rune_only_element(the list, the value).

the first element of a list is a value if
    prolog rune_first(the list, the value).

the last element of a list is a value if
    prolog rune_last(the list, the value).

% An input of one value or none: the value of a list of one, else nothing.
the value or nothing of a list is a value if
    prolog rune_or_nothing(the list, the value).

% Rune's min [key], max [key] and sort [key]: the second list holds the keys of
% the first list's elements, in the same order.
the element of a list with the least of the keys a second list is a value if
    prolog rune_min_by(the list, the second list, the value).

the element of a list with the greatest of the keys a second list is a value if
    prolog rune_max_by(the list, the second list, the value).

the elements of a list sorted by the keys a second list are a third list if
    prolog rune_sorted_by(the list, the second list, the third list).

% Rune's min and max.
the least of a list is a value if
    prolog rune_min(the list, the value).

the greatest of a list is a value if
    prolog rune_max(the list, the value).

% The values of the list, each once, in the order of their first appearance.
the distinct values of a list are a second list if
    prolog rune_distinct(the list, the second list).

the reverse of a list is a second list if
    prolog rune_reverse(the list, the second list).

the sorted values of a list are a second list if
    prolog rune_sorted(the list, the second list).

% Rune's + on texts.
the concatenation of a text and a second text is a third text if
    prolog rune_concat(the text, the second text, the third text).

the text of a value is a text if
    prolog rune_to_string(the value, the text).

the number of a value is a number if
    prolog rune_to_number(the value, the number).

% Rune's contains: neither list is empty, and the first has every element
% of the second.
a list contains every element of a second list if
    prolog rune_contains_all(the list, the second list).

% Rune's disjoint.
a list shares no element with a second list if
    prolog rune_disjoint(the list, the second list).

% The order of dates and times, written as ISO 8601 texts.
a value comes before a second value if
    prolog rune_earlier(the value, the second value).

the joining of a list with a separator is a text if
    prolog rune_join(the list, the separator, the text).

% Rune's Now, as DRR's tests run it: the reporting time of the test packs.
the time of the report is a time if
    prolog rune_now(the time).

% CDM's DayOfWeek.
the day of the week of a date is a day if
    prolog rune_day_of_week(the date, the day).

% CDM's AddDays, DateDifference and LeapYearDateDifference.
the date a date plus a number days is a second date if
    prolog rune_add_days(the date, the number, the second date).

the days from a date to a second date are a number if
    prolog rune_date_difference(the date, the second date, the number).

the leap days from a date to a second date are a number if
    prolog rune_leap_days(the date, the second date, the number).

% CDM's RoundToPrecision and RoundToSignificantFigures: Up, Down or Nearest.
the number a number rounded to a precision decimal places towards a direction is a value if
    prolog rune_round_to_precision(the number, the precision, the direction, the value).

the number a number rounded to a count significant figures towards a direction is a value if
    prolog rune_round_to_significant(the number, the count, the direction, the value).

% DRR's StringContains.
a text contains the text a second text if
    prolog rune_string_contains(the text, the second text).

% The object a Rune constructor builds, from the place it is built at and the
% values it is built from: the same object whenever they are the same.
the object built at a site is a value if
    prolog rune_object_0(the site, the value).

the object built at a site with an input is a value if
    prolog rune_object_1(the site, the input, the value).

the object built at a site with an input with a second input is a value if
    prolog rune_object_2(the site, the input, the second input, the value).

the object built at a site with an input with a second input with a third input is a value if
    prolog rune_object_3(the site, the input, the second input, the third input, the value).

the object built at a site with an input with a second input with a third input with a fourth input is a value if
    prolog rune_object_4(the site, the input, the second input, the third input, the fourth input, the value).

the object built at a site with an input with a second input with a third input with a fourth input with a fifth input is a value if
    prolog rune_object_5(the site, the input, the second input, the third input, the fourth input, the fifth input, the value).

the object built at a site with an input with a second input with a third input with a fourth input with a fifth input with a sixth input is a value if
    prolog rune_object_6(the site, the input, the second input, the third input, the fourth input, the fifth input, the sixth input, the value).

the object built at a site with an input with a second input with a third input with a fourth input with a fifth input with a sixth input with a seventh input is a value if
    prolog rune_object_7(the site, the input, the second input, the third input, the fourth input, the fifth input, the sixth input, the seventh input, the value).

the object built at a site with an input with a second input with a third input with a fourth input with a fifth input with a sixth input with a seventh input with an eighth input is a value if
    prolog rune_object_8(the site, the input, the second input, the third input, the fourth input, the fifth input, the sixth input, the seventh input, the eighth input, the value).

the date part of a time is a date if
    prolog rune_date_part(the time, the date).

the time part of a time is a time of day if
    prolog rune_time_part(the time, the time of day).

the time zone part of a time is a zone if
    prolog rune_timezone_part(the time, the zone).

the year part of a date is a year if
    prolog rune_year_part(the date, the year).

the month part of a date is a month if
    prolog rune_month_part(the date, the month).

the day part of a date is a day if
    prolog rune_day_part(the date, the day).
